      "chapter": "River Conservancy and Harbour Works",
      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Whangpoo Conservancy: major works since 1906]",
      "caption_extra": "Section: River Conservancy and Harbours. Whangpoo — Work Done: \"The major works have been:\" (lead-in printed at foot of p. 226)",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "No.",
            "Item"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(a)",
              "Left bank training wall at mouth, 1 mile long, of heavy marine type."
            ],
            [
              "(b)",
              "Closure of \"Old Ship Channel\" behind Gough Island, together with the deepening by training and dredging of the \"Old Junk Channel\" (now called Astraea Channel)."
            ],
            [
              "(c)",
              "Right bank training works at mouth."
            ],
            [
              "(d)",
              "Training works below \"Point\"."
            ],
            [
              "(e)",
              "Training works below Pootung Point."
            ],
            [
              "(f)",
              "Training works opposite Arsenal."
            ],
            [
              "(g)",
              "Numerous reclamations and bundings."
            ],
            [
              "(h)",
              "Special and maintenance dredging, amounting in all to over thirty-one million cubic yards, practically all of which has been pumped ashore."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Lettered list transcribed as a table per brief (lists count)."
