      "chapter": "River Conservancy and Harbour Works",
      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Shanghai Harbour: particulars]",
      "caption_extra": "Section: River Conservancy and Harbours. Shanghai Harbour",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "Item",
            "Particulars"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Wharves",
              "There are many wharves in Shanghai Harbour, all under private ownership. Arrangements regarding berthing at a wharf should be made with the owner thereof."
            ],
            [
              "Depth",
              "Vessels up to 24 feet can pass through the entire harbour at extreme Low Water. At High Water vessels of 32 feet draught can do so."
            ],
            [
              "No. of vessels that can be accommodated",
              "The harbour has accommodated 156 merchant vessels and 22 warships at one and the same time. The largest vessel to enter the harbour was 657 feet in length and 30 feet draught. She could be berthed at a wharf or head and stern mooring."
            ],
            [
              "Loading and Unloading",
              "Are done entirely by coolie labour. The capacity depends on number of men employed."
            ],
            [
              "No. of Berths",
              "There are 64 head and stern mooring berths in the stream including 4 naval berths, 4 berths for Customs cruisers and 2 berths for cable ships. Vessels may not moor with their own anchors in the harbour."
            ],
            [
              "Dry Docks",
              "See separate table (p0583_1)."
            ],
            [
              "Bunkering",
              "Coaling is effected entirely by hand labour from cargo boats, or wharves."
            ],
            [
              "Pilotage",
              "Pilotage is not compulsory. See separate table (p0583_2)."
            ],
            [
              "Harbour Dues",
              "All harbour dues are included in tonnage dues which are payable every four months at the rate of four mace per ton register by vessels of more than 150 tons, and one mace per ton by vessels of 150 tons or under."
            ],
            [
              "Berthing Charges",
              "See separate table (p0583_3)."
            ],
            [
              "Wharfage Dues",
              "See separate table (p0584_1)."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Run-in headed particulars (pp. 227–228) transcribed as a list-table per brief; the entries that carry their own tables are cross-referenced rather than repeated. 'See separate table' texts are transcriber's, not printed."
